From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lb2004 <lb2004@lb2004>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dma-buf: downgrade vmapping_counter BUG_ON to WARN_ON

The rknpu v0.9.8 driver on rk3566 triggers a vmap/vunmap imbalance
(dma_buf_vmap without matching dma_buf_vunmap before fd close) when
running large RKNN models. The imbalance only surfaces during process
exit (dma_buf_release), causing a fatal kernel panic that reboots the
board after every inference run.

Downgrade BUG_ON(dmabuf->vmapping_counter) to WARN_ON so the leak is
still reported but no longer kills the machine. This matches what
mainline Linux eventually did with these checks.

Signed-off-by: lb2004 <lb2004@lb2004>
---
 drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c b/drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c
+++ b/drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@ static void dma_buf_release(struct dentry *dentry)
 	if (unlikely(!dmabuf))
 		return;
 
-	BUG_ON(dmabuf->vmapping_counter);
+	WARN_ON(dmabuf->vmapping_counter);
 
 	/*
 	 * If you hit this BUG() it could mean:
-- 
2.34.1
